Using Convex 1.44.0, articles has title: string, content: string, author: string, tags: string[], isPublished: boolean and this search index:

```ts
.searchIndex("search_articles", {
  searchField: "content",
  filterFields: ["author", "isPublished"],
})
```

A query validates { searchTerm: string, author: string }. It must use native full-text search on content and return up to ten published matches belonging to that author. The handler is:

```ts
const articles = await ctx.db.query("articles")
  .withSearchIndex("search_articles", (q) =>
    /* Insert one option here. */)
  .take(10);
return articles.map((article) => ({
  title: article.title, author: article.author,
  preview: article.content.slice(0, 100), tags: article.tags,
}));
```
